# Project rules

The canonical, always-applicable rules for this repository live in **`/CLAUDE.md`** (Cursor
also reads the root `AGENTS.md`, which is a symlink to it). Read it in full before working.

`CLAUDE.md` is a **router**: start from its "Start here — context map" and load the
task-relevant files (`TODO.md`, `README.md` (`## Features`), the relevant `src/**` and its
`test/*.test.ts`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`) before acting. Do not work from this pointer or
from `CLAUDE.md` alone.

Hard rules to remember:
- **Design before code** — no implementation (not even tests) until the design is finished and
  any architectural decision is approved.
- **Doc-sync in the same change** — update README/CHANGELOG/TODO/Features when code changes; CI
  enforces it.
- **Zero runtime dependencies** — the GitLab API is called via Node's built-in `https`; a new
  runtime dependency needs a justified decision.
- **GitLab tokens are full-access credentials** — never log, hard-code, or commit them.
